From 97699d707df374773fe5d6e32ea7362ef8dcf51b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viorel Cernateanu <vrilutza@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 15:15:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] gstpipewiresrc: do not restart the stream when the running
 caps still fit

gst_pipewire_src_negotiate() already tries to skip renegotiation when nothing
changed, but it compared the fixed current caps against the first structure of
the peer's caps, which can still hold ranges. A fixed caps is never equal to a
range, so the check could not fire. Those ranges do not have to come from the
source: an ordinary videoconvert downstream is enough, so this hits pipelines
that have nothing unusual about them. Every reconfigure event travelling up then
disconnected the stream and connected it again with the format it already had.

Ask the question that is actually being asked instead: are the caps we are
already running still acceptable downstream? If they are, there is nothing to
renegotiate.

The plainest case is resizing a video window, where videoscale emits the
reconfigure itself and the source can stay on the format it has. Measured with
the display size changed three times and the source caps unchanged at 640x480
throughout: three gaps of 0.8 to 2.2 s before, none after. Sending the
reconfigure directly gives the same shape, as does a pipeline built like the one
GNOME Snapshot uses, where it comes from parsebin. On the camera this started
from, each restart costs about 1.3 s, because that driver spends roughly a
second inside VIDIOC_STREAMON.

A real format change still renegotiates: a running pipeline moved from 640x480
to 1280x720 switches with and without this patch.
Source: https://github.com/PipeWire/pipewire/commit/97699d707df374773fe5d6e32ea7362ef8dcf51b
---
 src/gst/gstpipewiresrc.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gst/gstpipewiresrc.c b/src/gst/gstpipewiresrc.c
index 72a939691..55f7c8fd7 100644
--- a/src/gst/gstpipewiresrc.c
+++ b/src/gst/gstpipewiresrc.c
@@ -1248,7 +1248,11 @@ gst_pipewire_src_negotiate (GstBaseSrc * basesrc)
     current_caps = gst_pad_get_current_caps (GST_BASE_SRC_PAD (pwsrc));
     preferred_new_caps = gst_caps_copy_nth (possible_caps, 0);
 
-    if (current_caps && gst_caps_is_equal (current_caps, preferred_new_caps)) {
+    /* The caps we are already running are still acceptable downstream: a reconfigure
+     * that does not actually ask for anything different should not cost a stream
+     * restart. Comparing against the peer's first structure alone is not enough,
+     * because it can still hold ranges and never compares equal to fixed caps. */
+    if (current_caps && gst_caps_is_subset (current_caps, possible_caps)) {
       GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (pwsrc,
                         "Stream running and new caps equal current ones. "
                         "Skipping renegotiation.");
